CORE
main.c
--dump-c
^#include <math.h>$
^  return fma\(x, x, 1\.0\);$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Invariant check failed
^warning: ignoring
--
--dump-c of a goto binary built by goto-cc printed __CPROVER_fma's
three-operand expression (the rounding mode is added later, by
adjust_float_expressions) and stopped with "Fused multiply-add must have
four operands".  The dump calls fma, whose declaration it now includes
(<math.h>), so that the dumped program compiles and verifies.
